Apple has announced that it is celebrating the 30th anniversary of Pokémon <a href="https://x.com/AppStoreJP/status/2122260990557618476">in a variety of ways</a> starting today — primarily in Japan.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Apple-Gift-Card-Special-Pokemon-Edition.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077728" /><br/>
First, Apple is selling Pokémon Special Edition gift cards featuring <a href="https://www.pokemon.com/us/pokedex/applin">Applin</a> until November 30 at all Apple Store locations in Japan. The cards can be loaded with ¥1,000 to ¥250,000, and there is a limit of three per customer while supplies last.<br/>
<br/>
Second, Apple has released a set of <a href="https://offers.applegiftcard.apple/pokemon">original Pokémon wallpapers for the iPhone</a>, including one for the iPhone Duo. The wallpapers can be downloaded <a href="https://offers.applegiftcard.apple/pokemon">here</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Apple-Pokemon-iPhone-Wallpapers.jpg" alt="" width="1464" height="823" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077726" /><br/>
Third, all Apple Store locations in Japan <a href="https://x.com/AppStoreJP/status/2122260992780648928">are PokéStops</a> in Pokémon GO until November 30.<br/>
<br/>
Fourth, Apple Stores in Japan have "We &#x2764;&#xfe0f; Pokémon" marketing.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/We-Love-Pokemon-Apple-Store-Japan-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="2560" height="1708" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077727" /><br/>
